=> Developed a Python script using subprocess to execute Linux df -h commands, parse filesystem output, and display disk capacity, used space, available space, utilization percentage, and mount point.

import subprocess

result = subprocess.run(
    ["df", "-h", "/"],
    capture_output=True,
    text=True
)

lines = result.stdout.splitlines()

data = lines[1].split()

filesystem = data[0]
size = data[1]
used = data[2]
available = data[3]
usage = data[4]
mount = data[5]

print("Filesystem:", filesystem)
print("Total Size:", size)
print("Used:", used)
print("Available:", available)
print("Usage:", usage)
print("Mounted on:", mount)

Output:

Filesystem: /dev/sda2
Total Size: 29G
Used: 14G
Available: 13G
Usage: 53%
Mounted on: /

